:"landmark","la":37.8025,"lo":-122.401389,"d":311,"ds":"Levi Strauss Plaza, also known as Levi Plaza or Levi's Plaza, is an office complex located in North Waterfront district of San Francisco, west of The Embarcadero. It houses the headquarters of Levi Strauss & Co. As of 1998 the company Blue Jeans Equity West is the landlord of the complex.","wpu":"Levi's Plaza","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Levi%27s_Plaza_%281155_Battery_001%29.jpg/960px-Levi%27s_Plaza_%281155_Battery_001%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Coit Tower","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.8025,"lo":-122.405833,"d":373,"ds":"Coit Tower ( KOYT; also known as Coit Memorial Tower) is a 210-foot (64 m) tower in the Telegraph Hill neighborhood of San Francisco, California, overlooking the city and San Francisco Bay. The tower, in the city's Pioneer Park, was built between 1932 and 1933 using Lillie Hitchcock Coit's bequest to beautify the city of San Francisco. It was added to the National Register of Historic Places on January 29, 2008.","wpu":"Coit Tower","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Coit_Tower_1.jpg/960px-Coit_Tower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Waterfront Park (San Francisco)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.80818,"lo":-122.40842,"d":593,"ds":"Waterfront Park is a park along San Francisco's Embarcadero, near Pier 39, in the U.S. state of California. The park, established in 1976, is owned by the Port Authority. The park is home to the Skygate sculpture.","wpu":"Waterfront Park (San Francisco)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Pier_-_panoramio_%2814%29.jpg/960px-Pier_-_panoramio_%2814%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"WonderCon","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.8,"lo":-122.4,"d":615,"ds":"WonderCon is an annual comic book, science fiction, and film convention. It was originally held in the San Francisco Bay Area (1987–2011), before moving to Anaheim, California under the name WonderCon Anaheim (2012–2015, 2017–present). Due to construction at the Anaheim Convention Center, the convention was held in Los Angeles in 2016 under the name WonderCon Los Angeles.","wpu":"WonderCon","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/WonderCon_2010_-_Floor_013.jpg/960px-WonderCon_2010_-_Floor_013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Liguria Bakery","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.8014,"lo":-122.4093,"d":683,"ds":"Liguria Bakery is a bakery in the North Beach neighborhood of San Francisco, California, United States that sells only focaccia. It is located on 1700 Stockton Street, at the corner of Filbert Street and across from Washington Square Park in North Beach.","wpu":"Liguria Bakery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Liguria_Bakery%2C_San_Francisco.jpg/960px-Liguria_Bakery%2C_San_Francisco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"The Anxious Asp","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.799812,"lo":-122.407947,"d":722,"ds":"The Anxious Asp was a lesbian and bohemian bar in operation from 1958 to 1967 at 528 Green Street in the North Beach neighborhood of San Francisco, California, U.S.","wpu":"The Anxious Asp","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/The_Anxious_Asp%2C_ca._1965.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Saints Peter and Paul Church, San Francisco","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.801603,"lo":-122.410197,"d":736,"ds":"Saints Peter and Paul Church (Italian: Ss. Pietro e Paolo, Chinese: 聖伯多禄圣保禄教堂) is a Catholic church in San Francisco's North Beach neighborhood. Located at 666 Filbert Street, it is directly across from Washington Square and is administered by the Salesians of Don Bosco.","wpu":"Saints Peter and Paul Church, San Francisco","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Saints_Peter_and_Paul_Church.JPG/960px-Saints_Peter_and_Paul_Church.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Statue of Benjamin Franklin (San Francisco)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.80082,"lo":-122.41,"d":770,"ds":"Benjamin Franklin – also known as the Benjamin Franklin Memorial, Benjamin Franklin Statue and Cogswell Historical Monument – is an outdoor sculpture in Washington Square, San Francisco, California.","wpu":"Statue of Benjamin Franklin (San Francisco)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/19/Benfranklinstatue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"San Francisco, officially the City and County of San Francisco, is the 17th-largest city and second-densest major city in the United States, with a 2025 population of 826,079. It is the fourth-most populous city in California and the second most-populous in the Bay Area. Some 4.6 million residents live in the city's metropolitan statistical area.","wpu":"San Francisco","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Zeppelin-ride-020100925-195_%285029394846%29.jpg/960px-Zeppelin-ride-020100925-195_%285029394846%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}